NAME
    rsudo-deploy — independent interactive deployment menu and CLI wrapper

SYNOPSIS
    rsudo-deploy
    rsudo-deploy operation [args...]

DESCRIPTION
    Without operands, starts the sourceable deployment menu.
    With operands, executes: rsudo deploy operation [args...].
    Native module entrypoint: rsudo [rsudo-options] deploy help.

    The first integration slice supports selecting an already loaded
    rsudo credential group, loading an encrypted credential file using the
    established m-core mechanism, and displaying CLI usage. Real deployment
    resource operations are not implemented yet.

    rsudo-admin's Deploy menu source-loads rsudo-deploy.lib.sh in a subshell,
    so groups already loaded into rsudo-admin remain available without export.
    An independently launched rsudo-deploy has its own shell and must load
    credential groups when needed.

SECURITY
    No new SSH/sudo or credential algorithm is provided. Remote administration
    continues to use the established rsudo interfaces. Never place secrets
    in plain deployment JSON.

STATUS
    Initial CLI/menu integration. Source builds and synthetic integration tests
    passed on Ubuntu and macOS; no new immutable release or live deployment
    has been accepted.

